module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Module.DepthSubsingleton
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.WeakAssPushforward
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.PushforwardRegularity.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Depth.HomRestriction

/-!
# Depth two for the pushforward at a point outside the image

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism of schemes, let `F` be a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module and let `s ∈ S` be a point outside the image of `f`. If the stalk
`(f_* F)_s` is a finite module over `𝒪_{S,s}` and `𝒪_{S,s}` is Noetherian, then

`depth ((f_* F)_s) ≥ 2`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0EY0] part (3), for a general quasi-compact quasi-separated morphism.

## The argument

The depth bound is the commutative-algebra criterion
`Module.two_le_depth_of_bijective_restrict_maximalIdeal`: it suffices that restriction

`Hom_{𝒪_{S,s}}(𝒪_{S,s}, (f_*F)_s) ⟶ Hom_{𝒪_{S,s}}(𝔪_s, (f_*F)_s)`

be bijective, which is the vanishing of `Hom(κ(s), (f_*F)_s)` and `Ext¹(κ(s), (f_*F)_s)` the
source reduces to.

The source proves that bijectivity by flat base change to `Spec 𝒪_{S,s}`, where `s` becomes a
closed point, so that `𝔪_s` generates the unit ideal on `X` and adjunction identifies
`Hom_{𝒪_S}(𝔪, f_*F)` with `Hom_{𝒪_X}(f^*𝔪, F) = Hom_{𝒪_X}(𝒪_X, F)`. Here that base change is
replaced by a covering statement proved directly on germs, exactly as parts (4) and (5) are
carried out on germs in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/PushforwardRegularity/Basic.lean`:

`exists_nbhd_mem_basicOpen`: for an affine open `V₀ ∋ s` there are a neighbourhood `V ≤ V₀` of
`s` and a *finite* set `bs` of sections of `𝒪_S` over `V₀`, all lying in the prime of `s`, whose
basic opens pull back to a cover of `f⁻¹V`.

This is the germ-level form of the source's covering `X = ⋃_{a ∈ 𝔪} f⁻¹D(a)` after base change.
Its proof is the one of [Stacks, Tag 0AVN]: on an affine chart `W ≤ f⁻¹V₀` the point `s` is not
in the image, so `exists_notMem_map_primeIdealOf` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Divisors/WeakAssPushforward.lean` produces `t ∉ 𝔭` whose pullback
lies in the ideal generated by `𝔭`; writing that pullback as a finite combination of pullbacks
of elements of `𝔭` and taking germs at a point of `W` over the basic open of `t`, one of those
elements must be invertible there, because the stalk is local. Quasi-compactness of `f⁻¹V₀`
assembles the finitely many charts into one neighbourhood of `s` and one finite set `bs`.

Both halves of the bijectivity then follow from the cover with no further input, and neither
needs the elements of `bs` to generate `𝔪_s`:

* `eq_zero_of_germ_smul_eq_zero`: an element of `(f_*F)_s` annihilated by the germs of all the
  `a ∈ bs` vanishes — a representing section has vanishing germ at every point of the cover,
  since some pullback is invertible there.
* `exists_germ_smul_eq`: values `μ a` prescribed on `bs` and compatible in the sense
  `b · μ a = a · μ b` are the multiples of a single element — on the basic open of `a` the
  representing section is divided by the pullback of `a`, the quotients agree on overlaps by the
  compatibility, and they glue.

For an arbitrary `x ∈ 𝔪_s` the difference between the two sides is annihilated by every `a ∈ bs`,
so the first bullet upgrades the second from `bs` to the whole maximal ideal.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.PushforwardRegularity.exists_nbhd_mem_basicOpen`: the covering that
  replaces the base change to `Spec 𝒪_{S,s}`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.PushforwardRegularity.two_le_depth_stalk_pushforward_of_notMem_range`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0EY0] part (3)**.

Part (1) of the same tag, that a point outside the image is not weakly associated to `f_* F`, is
[Stacks, Tag 0AVN], already proved as
`WeakAssPushforward.not_isWeaklyAssociatedPoint_pushforward_of_not_mem_range` under exactly the
hypotheses of part (1); the tag is attached to it here rather than restated.

## Implementation notes

The germ toolkit (`pushforwardGerm`, `stalkPullback`, `resF`, `exists_glue`, `section_ext_F`) is
the one set up for parts (4) and (5) in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/PushforwardRegularity/Basic.lean`.

Neither quasi-separatedness of `f` nor quasi-coherence of `F` is used; both are recorded because
the source assumes them.

`Module.depth` of a zero module is `⊤`, which is the degenerate case of the theorem.

The earlier `two_le_depth_stalk_of_isIso_unit_of_notMem` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/PushforwardRegularity/OutsideImageDepth.lean` proves the same
clause for an open immersion with `X` locally Noetherian; it is kept because its hypothesis is
the one its two consumers have, and its registration of the tag records that restriction.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EY0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EY0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AVN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AVN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.PushforwardRegularity

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.WeakAssPushforward

add_to_stacks 0EY0 "part (1)"
  WeakAssPushforward.not_isWeaklyAssociatedPoint_pushforward_of_not_mem_range

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (F : X.Modules)

/-! ### Two compatibilities of `f.appLE` with the germ at `s` of the pushforward -/

/-- Pulling a section of `𝒪_S` back from a large open to the preimage of a small one is the same
as restricting it first. -/
private lemma appLE_eq_app_res {V₀ V : S.Opens} (hV : V ≤ V₀) (hpre : f ⁻¹ᵁ V ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀)
    (a : Γ(S, V₀)) :
    f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) hpre a = f.app V (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op a) := by
  have h := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (f.map_appLE (U := V) (V := f ⁻¹ᵁ V) le_rfl (homOfLE hV).op) a
  rw [CommRingCat.comp_apply, f.appLE_eq_app] at h
  exact h.symm

/-- Restricting a section of `𝒪_X` twice is restricting it once. -/
private lemma res_res {U U' U'' : X.Opens} (h : U' ≤ U) (h' : U'' ≤ U') (a : Γ(X, U)) :
    X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op a) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h'.trans h)).op a := by
  rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← X.presheaf.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- `f.appLE` is the restriction of `f.app`. -/
private lemma appLE_eq_res {V₀ : S.Opens} {W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀) (a : Γ(S, V₀)) :
    f.appLE V₀ W hW a = X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op (f.app V₀ a) :=
  CommRingCat.comp_apply (f.app V₀) (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op) a

/-- The pullback of a section of `𝒪_S` is invertible on the pullback of its basic open. -/
private lemma isUnit_appLE_of_le_basicOpen {V₀ : S.Opens} (a : Γ(S, V₀)) {W : X.Opens}
    (hWb : W ≤ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ a)) (hW : W ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀) :
    IsUnit (f.appLE V₀ W hW a) := by
  have hb : IsUnit (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (f.app V₀ a))).op (f.app V₀ a)) :=
    RingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen _ (f.app V₀ a)
  have hm := hb.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWb).op).hom
  rw [res_res (X.basicOpen_le (f.app V₀ a)) hWb (f.app V₀ a)] at hm
  rwa [appLE_eq_res f hW a]

/-- Germs at `s` of the pushforward are additive. -/
private lemma pushforwardGerm_sub {s : S} {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) (ξ η : Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) :
    pushforwardGerm f F s V hsV (ξ - η) =
      pushforwardGerm f F s V hsV ξ - pushforwardGerm f F s V hsV η :=
  map_sub (TopCat.Presheaf.germ
    ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf V s hsV).hom ξ η

/-- Germs at `s` of the pushforward are compatible with the action of a section of `𝒪_S` over an
open containing the one the section of `F` lives over. -/
private lemma pushforwardGerm_smul_appLE {s : S} {V₀ V : S.Opens} (hV : V ≤ V₀) (hsV : s ∈ V)
    (hpre : f ⁻¹ᵁ V ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀) (a : Γ(S, V₀)) (ξ : Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) :
    pushforwardGerm f F s V hsV ((f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) hpre a) • ξ) =
      S.presheaf.germ V₀ s (hV hsV) a • pushforwardGerm f F s V hsV ξ := by
  rw [appLE_eq_app_res f hV hpre a, pushforwardGerm_smul f F s V hsV,
    S.presheaf.germ_res_apply (homOfLE hV) s hsV a]

/-! ### The covering that replaces the base change to `Spec 𝒪_{S,s}` -/

/-- Finitely many open neighbourhoods of `s` contain a common one inside any given neighbourhood. -/
private lemma exists_le_forall_le_of_finite {s : S} {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) {ι : Type*}
    [Finite ι] (V' : ι → S.Opens) (hs : ∀ i, s ∈ V' i) :
    ∃ V₁ : S.Opens, s ∈ V₁ ∧ V₁ ≤ V ∧ ∀ i, V₁ ≤ V' i :=
  ⟨V ⊓ ⨅ i, V' i, ⟨hsV, by simpa only [SetLike.mem_coe, Opens.coe_iInf, Set.mem_iInter] using hs⟩,
    inf_le_left, fun i => inf_le_right.trans (iInf_le _ i)⟩

/-- The covering statement on a single affine chart of `X`: over the basic open of a section `t`
invertible at `s`, every point of the chart lies in the pullback of the basic open of one of
finitely many sections of the prime of `s`. -/
private theorem exists_nbhd_mem_basicOpen_aux {s : S} (hrange : s ∉ Set.range f.base)
    {V₀ : S.Opens} (hV₀ : IsAffineOpen V₀) (hsV₀ : s ∈ V₀) {y : X} (hy : y ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀) :
    ∃ (W : X.Opens) (_ : y ∈ W) (_ : W ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀) (V' : S.Opens) (_ : s ∈ V')
      (bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀)),
      (∀ a ∈ bs, a ∈ (hV₀.primeIdealOf ⟨s, hsV₀⟩).asIdeal) ∧
        ∀ z ∈ W, f.base z ∈ V' → ∃ a ∈ bs, z ∈ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ a) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨W, hW, rfl⟩, hyW, hWsub⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hy (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀).isOpen
  have hWle : W ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ := hWsub
  obtain ⟨t, htp, htmem⟩ := exists_notMem_map_primeIdealOf f hrange hV₀ hsV₀ hW hWle
  obtain ⟨n, c, g, hsum⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_set'.mp htmem
  choose a hap hga using fun i : Fin n => (g i).2
  -- the pullback of `t` is the combination of the pullbacks of the `a i`
  have hsum' : ∑ i, c i * (f.appLE V₀ W hWle (a i)) = f.appLE V₀ W hWle t := by
    rw [← hsum]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by rw [hga i, smul_eq_mul]
  refine ⟨W, hyW, hWle, S.basicOpen t,
    mem_basicOpen_of_notMem_primeIdealOf hV₀ hsV₀ t htp, Finset.image a Finset.univ, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro b hb
    obtain ⟨i, -, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp hb
    exact hap i
  · intro z hzW hzt
    -- the germ at `z` of the pullback of `t` is a unit
    have hunit : IsUnit (X.presheaf.germ W z hzW (f.appLE V₀ W hWle t)) := by
      rw [germ_appLE f hWle t z hzW]
      refine (X.mem_basicOpen (f.app V₀ t) z (hWle hzW)).mp ?_
      rwa [← Scheme.preimage_basicOpen]
    by_contra hcon
    push Not at hcon
    -- otherwise every germ of a pullback of an `a i` is in the maximal ideal
    have hmemi : ∀ i : Fin n, X.presheaf.germ W z hzW (f.appLE V₀ W hWle (a i)) ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk z) := by
      intro i
      rw [germ_appLE f hWle (a i) z hzW, IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff]
      intro hu
      exact hcon (a i) (Finset.mem_image_of_mem a (Finset.mem_univ i))
        ((X.mem_basicOpen (f.app V₀ (a i)) z (hWle hzW)).mpr hu)
    -- so is the germ of the pullback of `t`, which contradicts its invertibility
    refine ((IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal _).mp ?_) hunit
    rw [← hsum', map_sum (X.presheaf.germ W z hzW).hom]
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
    rw [map_mul (X.presheaf.germ W z hzW).hom]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (hmemi i)

/-- **The covering that replaces the base change to `Spec 𝒪_{S,s}`.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be
quasi-compact, let `s ∈ S` be outside the image of `f` and let `V₀ ∋ s` be an affine open. Then
there are a neighbourhood `V ≤ V₀` of `s` and a finite set `bs` of sections of `𝒪_S` over `V₀`,
all in the prime ideal of `s`, such that the pullbacks of their basic opens cover `f⁻¹V`.

In the source this is the covering `X = ⋃_{a ∈ 𝔪} f⁻¹D(a)` of [Stacks, Tag 0AVN], available
there because `s` is a closed point after base change to `Spec 𝒪_{S,s}`. -/
public theorem exists_nbhd_mem_basicOpen [QuasiCompact f] {s : S}
    (hrange : s ∉ Set.range f.base) {V₀ : S.Opens} (hV₀ : IsAffineOpen V₀) (hsV₀ : s ∈ V₀) :
    ∃ (V : S.Opens) (_ : s ∈ V) (_ : V ≤ V₀) (bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀)),
      (∀ a ∈ bs, a ∈ (hV₀.primeIdealOf ⟨s, hsV₀⟩).asIdeal) ∧
        ∀ z ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V, ∃ a ∈ bs, z ∈ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ a) := by
  classical
  choose W hyW hWle V' hsV' bs hbsp hcov using fun y : (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ : X.Opens) =>
    exists_nbhd_mem_basicOpen_aux f hrange hV₀ hsV₀ y.2
  obtain ⟨T, hT⟩ := (f.isCompact_preimage hV₀.isCompact).elim_finite_subcover
    (fun y : (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ : X.Opens) => (W y : Set X)) (fun y => (W y).isOpen)
    fun z hz => Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨⟨z, hz⟩, hyW ⟨z, hz⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨V₁, hsV₁, hV₁V₀, hV₁⟩ := exists_le_forall_le_of_finite hsV₀
    (fun i : {x : (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ : X.Opens) // x ∈ T} => V' i.1) fun i => hsV' i.1
  refine ⟨V₁, hsV₁, hV₁V₀, T.biUnion bs, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro b hb
    obtain ⟨i, -, hbi⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp hb
    exact hbsp i b hbi
  · intro z hz
    have hz₀ : z ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ := hV₁V₀ hz
    obtain ⟨i, hi, hzi⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hT hz₀)
    obtain ⟨b, hb, hzb⟩ := hcov i z hzi (hV₁ ⟨i, hi⟩ hz)
    exact ⟨b, Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨i, hi, hb⟩, hzb⟩

/-! ### Shrinking the base -/

/-- Finitely many sections of `F` over `f⁻¹V` whose germs in the stalk of `f_* F` at `s` vanish
all restrict to zero over one neighbourhood of `s`. -/
private theorem exists_nbhd_resF_eq_zero {s : S} {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) {κ : Type u}
    [Finite κ] (ξ : κ → Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) (h : ∀ i, pushforwardGerm f F s V hsV (ξ i) = 0) :
    ∃ (V' : S.Opens) (_ : V' ≤ V) (_ : s ∈ V') (hpre : f ⁻¹ᵁ V' ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V),
      ∀ i, resF F hpre (ξ i) = 0 := by
  choose V₁ hsV₁ _ hV₁V hV₁V' he using fun i => TopCat.Presheaf.germ_eq_of_isBasis
    S.isBasis_affineOpens ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s hsV hsV
    ((h i).trans (pushforwardGerm_zero f F s V hsV).symm)
  obtain ⟨V₂, hsV₂, hV₂V, hV₂⟩ := exists_le_forall_le_of_finite hsV V₁ hsV₁
  refine ⟨V₂, hV₂V, hsV₂, fun _ hz => hV₂V hz, fun i => ?_⟩
  have hpre₁ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁ i := fun _ hz => hV₂ i hz
  have hpre₂ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁ i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V := fun _ hz => hV₁V i hz
  have hzero : resF F hpre₂ (ξ i) = 0 := by
    refine (he i).trans ?_
    exact map_zero (F.val.map (homOfLE (fun _ hz => hV₁V' i hz : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁ i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V)).op).hom
  rw [← resF_resF F hpre₂ hpre₁ (ξ i), hzero, resF_zero]

/-! ### The injectivity half -/

/-- **Injectivity.** An element of the stalk of `f_* F` at `s` annihilated by the germs of all the
sections of the cover is zero: a representing section has vanishing germ at every point of
`f⁻¹V`, because some pullback is invertible there. -/
private theorem eq_zero_of_germ_smul_eq_zero {s : S} {V₀ : S.Opens} (hsV₀ : s ∈ V₀)
    {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) (hVV₀ : V ≤ V₀) (bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀))
    (hcov : ∀ z ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V, ∃ a ∈ bs, z ∈ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ a))
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s)
    (hm : ∀ a ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a • m = 0) :
    m = 0 := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨V₁, hV₁V, hsV₁, ξ, hξ'⟩ : ∃ (V₁ : S.Opens) (_ : V₁ ≤ V) (hsV₁ : s ∈ V₁)
      (ξ : Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁)), pushforwardGerm f F s V₁ hsV₁ ξ = m := by
    obtain ⟨V₁, hV₁V, hsV₁, ξ, hξ⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_le_germ_eq
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf m hsV
    exact ⟨V₁, hV₁V, hsV₁, ξ, hξ⟩
  have hV₁V₀ : V₁ ≤ V₀ := hV₁V.trans hVV₀
  have hpre₁ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ := fun _ hz => hV₁V₀ hz
  -- the annihilation statements, as germs of sections over `f⁻¹V₁`
  obtain ⟨V₂, hV₂V₁, hsV₂, hpre₂, hzero⟩ := exists_nbhd_resF_eq_zero f F hsV₁
    (fun a : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} => (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁) hpre₁ a.1) • ξ) (by
      intro a
      rw [pushforwardGerm_smul_appLE f F hV₁V₀ hsV₁ hpre₁ a.1 ξ, hξ', hm a.1 a.2])
  have hV₂V₀ : V₂ ≤ V₀ := hV₂V₁.trans hV₁V₀
  have hpre₂₀ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ := fun _ hz => hV₂V₀ hz
  have hV₂V : V₂ ≤ V := hV₂V₁.trans hV₁V
  have hpre₂V : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V := fun _ hz => hV₂V hz
  -- the same, as equations of sections over `f⁻¹V₂`
  have hzero' : ∀ a ∈ bs, (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ a) • resF F hpre₂ ξ = 0 := by
    intro a ha
    rw [← resF_smul_appLE f F hpre₁ hpre₂ a ξ]
    exact hzero ⟨a, ha⟩
  -- the representative vanishes, because some pullback is invertible at each point
  have hvanish : resF F hpre₂ ξ = 0 := by
    refine section_ext_F F _ _ fun z hz => ?_
    obtain ⟨a, ha, hza⟩ := hcov z (hpre₂V hz)
    have hu : IsUnit (stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) a) :=
      (X.mem_basicOpen (f.app V₀ a) z (hpre₂₀ hz)).mp hza
    have hkill : stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) a •
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz (resF F hpre₂ ξ) = 0 := by
      rw [← germ_smul_appLE f F hpre₂₀ a (resF F hpre₂ ξ) z hz, hzero' a ha]
      exact germF_zero F z hz
    rw [germF_zero F z hz]
    exact hu.smul_eq_zero.mp hkill
  have hres : pushforwardGerm f F s V₂ hsV₂ (resF F hpre₂ ξ) =
      pushforwardGerm f F s V₁ hsV₁ ξ := pushforwardGerm_res f F s hV₂V₁ hsV₂ hpre₂ ξ
  rw [← hξ', ← hres, hvanish]
  exact pushforwardGerm_zero f F s V₂ hsV₂

/-! ### The surjectivity half -/

/-- Values prescribed on the sections of the cover and compatible in the sense
`b · μ a = a · μ b` are the germs of sections over the preimage of one neighbourhood of `s`
satisfying the compatibility as equations of sections. -/
private theorem exists_nbhd_smul_comm_sections {s : S} {V₀ : S.Opens} (hsV₀ : s ∈ V₀)
    {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) (hVV₀ : V ≤ V₀) (bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀))
    (μ : Γ(S, V₀) → TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s)
    (hμ : ∀ a ∈ bs, ∀ b ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ b • μ a =
      S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a • μ b) :
    ∃ (V₂ : S.Opens) (hsV₂ : s ∈ V₂) (_ : V₂ ≤ V) (hpre₂₀ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀)
      (η : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} → Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂)),
      (∀ i j, (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ j.1) • η i =
        (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ i.1) • η j) ∧
      ∀ i, pushforwardGerm f F s V₂ hsV₂ (η i) = μ i.1 := by
  classical
  -- represent the prescribed values by sections over one neighbourhood of `s`
  choose V' hV'V hsV' ξ' hξ' using fun i : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} =>
    TopCat.Presheaf.exists_le_germ_eq
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf (μ i.1) hsV
  obtain ⟨V₁, hsV₁, hV₁V, hV₁V'⟩ := exists_le_forall_le_of_finite hsV V' hsV'
  have hV₁V₀ : V₁ ≤ V₀ := hV₁V.trans hVV₀
  have hpre₁ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ := fun _ hz => hV₁V₀ hz
  obtain ⟨ξ, hξg⟩ : ∃ ξ : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} → Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁),
      ∀ i, pushforwardGerm f F s V₁ hsV₁ (ξ i) = μ i.1 :=
    ⟨fun i => resF F (fun _ hz => hV₁V' i hz) (ξ' i),
      fun i => (pushforwardGerm_res f F s (hV₁V' i) hsV₁ _ (ξ' i)).trans (hξ' i)⟩
  -- the compatibilities hold as equations of sections after shrinking once more
  obtain ⟨V₂, hV₂V₁, hsV₂, hpre₂, hrel⟩ := exists_nbhd_resF_eq_zero f F hsV₁
    (fun q : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} × {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} =>
      (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁) hpre₁ q.2.1) • ξ q.1 -
        (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₁) hpre₁ q.1.1) • ξ q.2) (by
      intro q
      rw [pushforwardGerm_sub f F hsV₁,
        pushforwardGerm_smul_appLE f F hV₁V₀ hsV₁ hpre₁ q.2.1 (ξ q.1),
        pushforwardGerm_smul_appLE f F hV₁V₀ hsV₁ hpre₁ q.1.1 (ξ q.2), hξg q.1, hξg q.2,
        hμ q.1.1 q.1.2 q.2.1 q.2.2, sub_self])
  refine ⟨V₂, hsV₂, hV₂V₁.trans hV₁V, fun _ hz => (hV₂V₁.trans hV₁V₀) hz,
    fun i => resF F hpre₂ (ξ i), fun i j => ?_, fun i =>
      (pushforwardGerm_res f F s hV₂V₁ hsV₂ hpre₂ (ξ i)).trans (hξg i)⟩
  have h := hrel (i, j)
  rwa [resF_sub F hpre₂, resF_smul_appLE f F hpre₁ hpre₂ j.1 (ξ i),
    resF_smul_appLE f F hpre₁ hpre₂ i.1 (ξ j), sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- Sections of `F` over the pieces of a cover of `f⁻¹V₂` lying in the pullbacks of basic opens,
obtained by dividing compatible sections by the pullbacks, agree on overlaps. -/
private lemma resF_inf_eq_of_appLE_smul_eq {V₀ V₂ : S.Opens} (hpre₂₀ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀)
    {bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀)} (η : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} → Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂))
    (hrel₂ : ∀ i j, (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ j.1) • η i =
      (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ i.1) • η j)
    (U : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} → X.Opens) (hUle : ∀ i, U i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂)
    (hUb : ∀ i, U i ≤ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ i.1)) (hUV₀ : ∀ i, U i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀)
    (ζ : ∀ i, Γ(F, U i))
    (hζ : ∀ i, (f.appLE V₀ (U i) (hUV₀ i) i.1) • ζ i = resF F (hUle i) (η i))
    (i j : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs}) :
    resF F (inf_le_left : U i ⊓ U j ≤ U i) (ζ i) =
      resF F (inf_le_right : U i ⊓ U j ≤ U j) (ζ j) := by
  have hij : U i ⊓ U j ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ := inf_le_left.trans (hUV₀ i)
  have key : ∀ (k : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs}) (h : U i ⊓ U j ≤ U k),
      IsUnit (f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij k.1) ∧
        (f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij k.1) • resF F h (ζ k) =
          resF F (inf_le_left.trans (hUle i) : U i ⊓ U j ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) (η k) := fun k h =>
    ⟨isUnit_appLE_of_le_basicOpen f k.1 (h.trans (hUb k)) hij, by
      rw [← resF_smul_appLE f F (hUV₀ k) h k.1 (ζ k), hζ k, resF_resF F (hUle k) h (η k)]⟩
  obtain ⟨hiu, hi⟩ := key i inf_le_left
  obtain ⟨hju, hj⟩ := key j inf_le_right
  have hr := congrArg (resF F (inf_le_left.trans (hUle i) : U i ⊓ U j ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂)) (hrel₂ i j)
  rw [resF_smul_appLE f F hpre₂₀ (inf_le_left.trans (hUle i) : U i ⊓ U j ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) j.1 (η i),
    resF_smul_appLE f F hpre₂₀ (inf_le_left.trans (hUle i) : U i ⊓ U j ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) i.1 (η j)]
    at hr
  refine (hiu.mul hju).smul_left_cancel.mp ?_
  calc ((f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij i.1) * (f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij j.1)) •
        resF F (inf_le_left : U i ⊓ U j ≤ U i) (ζ i)
      = (f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij j.1) •
          resF F (inf_le_left.trans (hUle i) : U i ⊓ U j ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) (η i) := by
        rw [mul_comm, mul_smul, hi]
    _ = (f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij i.1) •
          resF F (inf_le_left.trans (hUle i) : U i ⊓ U j ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) (η j) := hr
    _ = ((f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij i.1) * (f.appLE V₀ (U i ⊓ U j) hij j.1)) •
          resF F (inf_le_right : U i ⊓ U j ≤ U j) (ζ j) := by
        rw [mul_smul, hj]

/-- The section glued from the quotients of compatible sections by the pullbacks recovers each of
them on multiplying back. -/
private lemma appLE_smul_glue_eq {V₀ V₂ : S.Opens} (hpre₂₀ : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀)
    {bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀)} (η : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} → Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂))
    (hrel₂ : ∀ i j, (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ j.1) • η i =
      (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ i.1) • η j)
    (U : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} → X.Opens) (hUle : ∀ i, U i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂)
    (hUb : ∀ i, U i ≤ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ i.1)) (hUV₀ : ∀ i, U i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀)
    (hcover : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ ⨆ i, U i) (ζ : ∀ i, Γ(F, U i))
    (hζ : ∀ i, (f.appLE V₀ (U i) (hUV₀ i) i.1) • ζ i = resF F (hUle i) (η i))
    (η₀ : Γ(F, f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂)) (hη₀ : ∀ i, resF F (hUle i) η₀ = ζ i) {a : Γ(S, V₀)} (ha : a ∈ bs) :
    (f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ a) • η₀ = η ⟨a, ha⟩ := by
  refine section_ext_F F _ _ fun z hz => ?_
  obtain ⟨j, hzj⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.mp (hcover hz)
  have hju : IsUnit (stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) j.1) :=
    (X.mem_basicOpen (f.app V₀ j.1) z (hpre₂₀ hz)).mp (hUb j hzj)
  refine hju.smul_left_cancel.mp ?_
  have hη₀g : TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz η₀ =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (U j) z hzj (ζ j) := by
    rw [← hη₀ j, germ_resF F (hUle j) η₀ z hzj]
  have hζj : stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) j.1 •
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (U j) z hzj (ζ j) =
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz (η j) := by
    rw [← germ_smul_appLE f F (hUV₀ j) j.1 (ζ j) z hzj, hζ j,
      germ_resF F (hUle j) (η j) z hzj]
  have hL : stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) j.1 •
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz
        ((f.appLE V₀ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) hpre₂₀ a) • η₀) =
      stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) a •
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz (η j) := by
    rw [germ_smul_appLE f F hpre₂₀ a η₀ z hz, smul_smul, mul_comm, ← smul_smul, hη₀g, hζj]
  have hR : stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) j.1 •
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz (η ⟨a, ha⟩) =
      stalkPullback f V₀ z (hpre₂₀ hz) a •
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz (η j) := by
    have h := congrArg (TopCat.Presheaf.germ F.val.presheaf (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) z hz)
      (hrel₂ ⟨a, ha⟩ j)
    rwa [germ_smul_appLE f F hpre₂₀ j.1 (η ⟨a, ha⟩) z hz,
      germ_smul_appLE f F hpre₂₀ a (η j) z hz] at h
  rw [hL, hR]

/-- **Surjectivity.** Values prescribed on the sections of the cover and compatible in the sense
`b · μ a = a · μ b` are the multiples of a single element of the stalk of `f_* F` at `s`.

On the pullback of the basic open of `a` the representing section is divided by the pullback of
`a`; the quotients agree on overlaps by the compatibility, so they glue to a section over
`f⁻¹V₂`. -/
private theorem exists_germ_smul_eq {s : S} {V₀ : S.Opens} (hsV₀ : s ∈ V₀)
    {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) (hVV₀ : V ≤ V₀) (bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀))
    (hcov : ∀ z ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V, ∃ a ∈ bs, z ∈ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ a))
    (μ : Γ(S, V₀) → TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s)
    (hμ : ∀ a ∈ bs, ∀ b ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ b • μ a =
      S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a • μ b) :
    ∃ m, ∀ a ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a • m = μ a := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨V₂, hsV₂, hV₂V, hpre₂₀, η, hrel₂, hηg⟩ :=
    exists_nbhd_smul_comm_sections f F hsV₀ hsV hVV₀ bs μ hμ
  have hpre₂V : f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V := fun _ hz => hV₂V hz
  -- the cover of `f⁻¹V₂` by the pullbacks of the basic opens
  obtain ⟨U, hUle, hUb, hcover⟩ : ∃ U : {a : Γ(S, V₀) // a ∈ bs} → X.Opens,
      (∀ i, U i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) ∧ (∀ i, U i ≤ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ i.1)) ∧
        f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂ ≤ ⨆ i, U i := by
    refine ⟨fun i => (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) ⊓ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ i.1), fun _ => inf_le_left,
      fun _ => inf_le_right, fun z hz => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨a, ha, hza⟩ := hcov z (hpre₂V hz)
    exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, ⟨hz, hza⟩⟩
  have hUV₀ : ∀ i, U i ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V₀ := fun i => (hUle i).trans hpre₂₀
  -- divide the representative by the pullback on each piece of the cover
  obtain ⟨ζ, hζ⟩ : ∃ ζ : ∀ i, Γ(F, U i),
      ∀ i, (f.appLE V₀ (U i) (hUV₀ i) i.1) • ζ i = resF F (hUle i) (η i) := by
    choose ζ hζ using fun i => (isUnit_appLE_of_le_basicOpen f i.1 (hUb i) (hUV₀ i)).exists_left_inv
    exact ⟨fun i => ζ i • resF F (hUle i) (η i),
      fun i => by rw [smul_smul, mul_comm, hζ i, one_smul]⟩
  -- glue the quotients, which agree on overlaps
  obtain ⟨η₀, hη₀⟩ := exists_glue F (f ⁻¹ᵁ V₂) U hcover hUle ζ
    (resF_inf_eq_of_appLE_smul_eq f F hpre₂₀ η hrel₂ U hUle hUb hUV₀ ζ hζ)
  refine ⟨pushforwardGerm f F s V₂ hsV₂ η₀, fun a ha => ?_⟩
  rw [← pushforwardGerm_smul_appLE f F (hV₂V.trans hVV₀) hsV₂ hpre₂₀ a η₀,
    appLE_smul_glue_eq f F hpre₂₀ η hrel₂ U hUle hUb hUV₀ hcover ζ hζ η₀ hη₀ ha]
  exact hηg ⟨a, ha⟩

/-- Restriction `Hom(𝒪_{S,s}, (f_*F)_s) → Hom(𝔪_s, (f_*F)_s)` is injective. -/
private theorem restrict_maximalIdeal_injective {s : S} {V₀ : S.Opens} (hsV₀ : s ∈ V₀)
    {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) (hVV₀ : V ≤ V₀) (bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀))
    (hmemM : ∀ a ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s))
    (hcov : ∀ z ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V, ∃ a ∈ bs, z ∈ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ a)) :
    Function.Injective fun g : S.presheaf.stalk s →ₗ[S.presheaf.stalk s]
        TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
          ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s =>
      g.comp (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s)).subtype := by
  intro g₁ g₂ hg
  refine LinearMap.ext_ring ?_
  have hone : ∀ g : S.presheaf.stalk s →ₗ[S.presheaf.stalk s]
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s,
      ∀ a : S.presheaf.stalk s, g a = a • g 1 := by
    intro g a
    conv_lhs => rw [← mul_one a, ← smul_eq_mul]
    exact map_smul g a 1
  have hsub : ∀ a ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a • (g₁ 1 - g₂ 1) = 0 := by
    intro a ha
    have h : g₁ (S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a) = g₂ (S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a) := by
      simpa only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.coe_subtype] using
        LinearMap.congr_fun hg ⟨S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a, hmemM a ha⟩
    rw [smul_sub, ← hone g₁, ← hone g₂, h, sub_self]
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp
    (eq_zero_of_germ_smul_eq_zero f F hsV₀ hsV hVV₀ bs hcov (g₁ 1 - g₂ 1) hsub)

/-- Restriction `Hom(𝒪_{S,s}, (f_*F)_s) → Hom(𝔪_s, (f_*F)_s)` is surjective. -/
private theorem restrict_maximalIdeal_surjective {s : S} {V₀ : S.Opens} (hsV₀ : s ∈ V₀)
    {V : S.Opens} (hsV : s ∈ V) (hVV₀ : V ≤ V₀) (bs : Finset Γ(S, V₀))
    (hmemM : ∀ a ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s))
    (hcov : ∀ z ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ V, ∃ a ∈ bs, z ∈ X.basicOpen (f.app V₀ a)) :
    Function.Surjective fun g : S.presheaf.stalk s →ₗ[S.presheaf.stalk s]
        TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
          ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s =>
      g.comp (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s)).subtype := by
  classical
  intro φ
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_germ_smul_eq f F hsV₀ hsV hVV₀ bs hcov
    (fun a => if ha : a ∈ bs then φ ⟨S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a, hmemM a ha⟩ else 0) (by
      intro a ha b hb
      rw [dite_eq_left ha, dite_eq_left hb, ← map_smul, ← map_smul]
      congr 1
      refine Subtype.ext ?_
      simpa only [SetLike.val_smul, smul_eq_mul] using mul_comm _ _)
  refine ⟨LinearMap.toSpanSingleton (S.presheaf.stalk s) _ m, ?_⟩
  -- the difference is annihilated by every section of the cover, hence vanishes
  set d := (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton (S.presheaf.stalk s) (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s) m).comp
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s)).subtype - φ with hd
  have hdgen : ∀ a (ha : a ∈ bs),
      d ⟨S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a, hmemM a ha⟩ = 0 := by
    intro a ha
    have hval : S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a • m =
        φ ⟨S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a, hmemM a ha⟩ := by
      rw [hm a ha, dite_eq_left ha]
    rw [hd]
    simpa only [LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.coe_subtype,
      LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply, sub_eq_zero] using hval
  have hdzero : ∀ x : ↥(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s)), d x = 0 := by
    intro x
    refine eq_zero_of_germ_smul_eq_zero f F hsV₀ hsV hVV₀ bs hcov (d x) fun a ha => ?_
    have hswap : (S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a) • x =
        (x : S.presheaf.stalk s) • (⟨S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a, hmemM a ha⟩ :
          ↥(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s))) := by
      refine Subtype.ext ?_
      simpa only [SetLike.val_smul, smul_eq_mul] using mul_comm _ _
    calc S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a • d x
        = d ((S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a) • x) := (map_smul d _ x).symm
      _ = d ((x : S.presheaf.stalk s) • (⟨S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a, hmemM a ha⟩ :
            ↥(IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s)))) := congrArg d hswap
      _ = (x : S.presheaf.stalk s) • d ⟨S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a, hmemM a ha⟩ :=
            map_smul d _ _
      _ = 0 := by rw [hdgen a ha, smul_zero]
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  have := hdzero x
  rw [hd] at this
  simpa only [LinearMap.sub_apply, sub_eq_zero] using this

/-! ### Tag 0EY0, part (3) -/

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0EY0] part (3).** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated
morphism of schemes and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module. Let `s ∈ S` be a point outside
the image of `f`. If `(f_* F)_s` is a finite `𝒪_{S,s}`-module and `𝒪_{S,s}` is Noetherian, then

`depth ((f_* F)_s) ≥ 2`.

Restriction `Hom(𝒪_{S,s}, (f_*F)_s) → Hom(𝔪_s, (f_*F)_s)` is bijective, which is the criterion
`Module.two_le_depth_of_bijective_restrict_maximalIdeal`; its two halves are
`eq_zero_of_germ_smul_eq_zero` and `exists_germ_smul_eq`, both fed by the covering
`exists_nbhd_mem_basicOpen` that replaces the source's base change to `Spec 𝒪_{S,s}`. -/
@[stacks 0EY0 "part (3)"]
public theorem two_le_depth_stalk_pushforward_of_notMem_range [QuasiCompact f] [QuasiSeparated f]
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] (s : S) (hs : s ∉ Set.range f)
    (hnoeth : IsNoetherianRing (S.presheaf.stalk s))
    (hfinite : Module.Finite (S.presheaf.stalk s) (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s)) :
    (2 : ℕ∞) ≤ Module.depth (S.presheaf.stalk s)
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s))
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s) := by
  classical
  have _ : IsNoetherianRing (S.presheaf.stalk s) := hnoeth
  have _ : Module.Finite (S.presheaf.stalk s) (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
    ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s) := hfinite
  by_cases htriv : Subsingleton (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s)
  · rw [Module.depth_eq_top_of_subsingleton]
    exact le_top
  have _ : Nontrivial (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
      ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward f).obj F).val.presheaf s) :=
    not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial.mp htriv
  -- an affine neighbourhood of `s`, and the cover of its preimage
  obtain ⟨-, ⟨V₀, hV₀, rfl⟩, hsV₀, -⟩ :=
    S.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ s) isOpen_univ
  have hV₀' : IsAffineOpen V₀ := hV₀
  obtain ⟨V, hsV, hVV₀, bs, hbsp, hcov⟩ := exists_nbhd_mem_basicOpen f hs hV₀' hsV₀
  have hmemM : ∀ a ∈ bs, S.presheaf.germ V₀ s hsV₀ a ∈
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (S.presheaf.stalk s) :=
    fun a ha => (germ_mem_maximalIdeal_iff hV₀' hsV₀ a).mpr (hbsp a ha)
  exact Module.two_le_depth_of_bijective_restrict_maximalIdeal _
    ⟨restrict_maximalIdeal_injective f F hsV₀ hsV hVV₀ bs hmemM hcov,
      restrict_maximalIdeal_surjective f F hsV₀ hsV hVV₀ bs hmemM hcov⟩

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.PushforwardRegularity

